      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Intrabiliary rupture of a hydatid liver cyst is infrequently reported, but may present with symptoms of choledocholethiasis or cholangitis. We report a case of hydatid liver disease presenting as recurrent pancreatitis, and discuss its clinical, radiological and surgical treatments. Hydatid liver disease has a diverse clinical spectrum, and a diagnosis of acute pancreatitis should be considered in patients with hydatid liver disease presenting with unexplained abdominal pain."},
